\"all\">All</option></select></label><label>Search<input data-search type=\"search\" placeholder=\"Rule, title or file\"></label><label>Severity<select data-severity><option value=\"\">All severities</option>\n<option value=\"critical\">critical</option>\n<option value=\"high\">high</option>\n<option value=\"medium\">medium</option>\n<option value=\"low\">low</option>\n<option value=\"info\">info</option>\n</select></label><label>Risk<select data-risk><option value=\"\">All risks</option>\n<option value=\"quantum-vulnerable\">quantum-vulnerable</option>\n<option value=\"quantum-uncertain\">quantum-uncertain</option>\n<option value=\"quantum-safe\">quantum-safe</option>\n<option value=\"non-quantum-risk\">non-quantum-risk</option>\n</select></label><button type=\"button\" data-reset>Reset</button></section><noscript><p>JavaScript is unavailable. All findings are shown below; native details still work. Interactive filters and pagination are unavailable.</p></noscript><p data-report-status role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p><p data-empty hidden>No matches. Change the view or filters; this does not mean the entire scan found nothing.</p><nav data-group-pager hidden aria-label=\"Rule pages\"><button type=\"button\" data-prev>Previous</button><span data-page></span><button type=\"button\" data-next>Next</button></nav>\n<details class=\"rule-card\" id=\"rule-0\" data-rule data-page-size=\"20\"><summary><span><strong>Synthetic migration reference</strong> <code>ENVOY056</code></span><span class=\"sev medium\">medium</span><span class=\"count\">1 hits</span><span>Files 1 / matches <span data-match-count></span></span></summary><div class=\"rule-body\"><p>Review actual use before migration</p>\n<h4>Locations and next steps</h4><nav data-occ-pager hidden><button type=\"button\" data-occ-prev>Previous locations</button><span data-occ-status aria-live=\"polite\"></span><button type=\"button\" data-occ-next>Next locations</button></nav><div data-occurrence-list>\n<details class=\"occurrence\" id=\"finding-0\" data-finding-id=\"ENVOY056\" data-inventory=\"false\" data-severity=\"medium\" data-risk=\"quantum-vulnerable\" data-search=\"ENVOY056 Synthetic migration reference envoy.yaml\"><summary><code>envoy.yaml:1:1</code><span class=\"occ-match\">synthetic reference</span><span class=\"next-step\">Next: Prefer TLS 1.3 and review legacy key exchange</span></summary><p>Risk: quantum-vulnerable</p><p>Check: Review actual use before migration</p><p>Evidence: <code>synthetic reference</code></p>\n<p>Source context unavailable; inspect the original file.</p>\n<h4>Recommended Actions</h4>\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>Validate Envoy PQC signature compatibility in control/data planes <span class=\"badge\">advisory</span></h4><p>Envoy TLS behavior depends on configured providers and peer capabilities; PQC signature readiness can vary between mesh edges, sidecars, and external clients.</p><ol>\n<li>Harden min/max TLS versions and retire static RSA key exchange where configured; ECDHE_RSA uses RSA authentication, not static RSA key exchange.</li>\n<li>Review cipher_suites for TLS 1.0-1.2, not TLS 1.3; review certificate signatures and peer compatibility separately.</li>\n<li>Verify PQC certificate-signature compatibility in both downstream and upstream clusters.</li>\n<li>Gate production rollout with staged canary tests and explicit fallback paths.</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>References and examples</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/intro/arch_overview/security/ssl.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/intro/arch_overview/security/ssl.html</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>Prefer TLS 1.3 and review legacy key exchange <span class=\"badge\">near-term</span></h4><p>RSA key exchange and legacy protocol versions are high-priority migration blockers for PQC readiness.</p><ol>\n<li>Prefer TLS 1.3; restrict connections to TLS 1.3 when all peers support it. Disable TLS 1.0 and 1.1.</li>\n<li>Retain securely configured TLS 1.2 only where interoperability requires it, and record the compatibility reason.</li>\n<li>Prefer ECDHE today and plan hybrid KEM suites for next phase.</li>\n<li>Continuously test interoperability across clients and load balancers.</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>References and examples</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>Set modern TLS policy in Envoy <span class=\"badge\">near-term</span></h4><p>Envoy control-plane config supports strict min/max protocol and cipher suite policy.</p><ol>\n<li>Prefer `tls_minimum_protocol_version: TLSv1_3`; use TLSv1_2 only when interoperability requires it.</li>\n<li>Review `cipher_suites` for TLS 1.0-1.2, not TLS 1.3. Retire static RSA key exchange where configured; ECDHE_RSA uses RSA authentication, not static RSA key exchange.</li>\n<li>Review certificate-signature migration and peer compatibility separately before removing RSA authentication.</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>References and examples</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n<p>Shared checks and planning (not verified facts about this line):</p><ul>\n<li><a href=\"#shared-0-0\">Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n</div>\n<details class=\"shared\"><summary>Shared checks and planning (1)</summary>\n<section id=\"shared-0-0\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan <span class=\"badge\">near-term</span></h4><p>The detected primitive is vulnerable to cryptographically relevant quantum attacks. Hybrid rollout minimizes compatibility risk.</p><ol>\n<li>Inventory all call sites using this algorithm and owner teams.</li>\n<li>Check for an existing classical + PQC composition; if migration is needed, evaluate compatible staged or hybrid modes before hard cut-over.</li>\n<li>Define retirement dates for legacy classical algorithms.</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>References and examples</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n</section>\n</details>\n</div></details>\n<details class=\"rule-card\" id=\"rule-1\" data-rule data-page-size=\"20\"><summary><span><strong>Synthetic migration reference</strong> <code>JAVA_CURRENT056</code></span><span class=\"sev medium\">medium</span><span class=\"count\">1 hits</span><span>Files 1 / matches <span data-match-count></span></span></summary><div class=\"rule-body\"><p>Review actual use before migration</p>\n<h4>Locations and next steps</h4><nav data-occ-pager hidden><button type=\"button\" data-occ-prev>Previous locations</button><span data-occ-status aria-live=\"polite\"></span><button type=\"button\" data-occ-next>Next locations</button></nav><div data-occurrence-list>\n<details class=\"occurrence\" id=\"finding-1\" data-finding-id=\"JAVA_CURRENT056\" data-inventory=\"false\" data-severity=\"medium\" data-risk=\"quantum-vulnerable\" data-search=\"JAVA_CURRENT056 Synthetic migration reference current/Example.java\"><summary><code>current/Example.java:1:1</code><span class=\"occ-match\">synthetic reference</span><span class=\"next-step\">Next: Use Java standard JCA names for ML-DSA / ML-KEM</span></summary><p>Risk: quantum-vulnerable</p><p>Check: Review actual use before migration</p><p>Evidence: <code>synthetic reference</code></p>\n<p>Source context unavailable; inspect the original file.</p>\n<h4>Recommended Actions</h4>\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>Use Java standard JCA names for ML-DSA / ML-KEM <span class=\"badge\">near-term</span></h4><p>Modern JDKs expose standardized PQC algorithm names through JCA, reducing vendor lock-in.</p><ol>\n<li>Select an explicit parameter set and generate a new ML-DSA key pair; never reuse RSA key material.</li>\n<li>Provision matching public keys and required JOSE/PKI encodings to all verifiers before switching signers to ML-DSA where policy allows.</li>\n<li>Adopt ML-KEM for key establishment in hybrid TLS/key exchange designs.</li>\n<li>Keep dual verification during migration to preserve compatibility.</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>References and examples</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://openjdk.org/jeps/496\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://openjdk.org/jeps/496</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://openjdk.org/jeps/497\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://openjdk.org/jeps/497</a></p>\n<p>Before (java)</p><pre><code>Signature sig = Signature.getInstance(&quot;SHA256withRSA&quot;);\nsig.initSign(privateKey);\nsig.update(payload);\nbyte[] signature = sig.sign();</code></pre><p>After</p><pre><code>// JDK 24+: provision a new ML-DSA key pair for the selected parameter set.\n// mlDsaPrivateKey is its private key, never the previous RSA key.\n// Provision the matching public key and encoding to verifiers before rollout.\nSignature sig = Signature.getInstance(&quot;ML-DSA&quot;);\nsig.initSign(mlDsaPrivateKey);\nsig.update(payload);\nbyte[] signature = sig.sign();\n// Keep legacy verification only under the explicit migration policy.</code></pre>\n</details>\n</section>\n<p>Shared checks and planning (not verified facts about this line):</p><ul>\n<li><a href=\"#shared-1-0\">Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#shared-1-1\">Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n</div>\n<details class=\"shared\"><summary>Shared checks and planning (2)</summary>\n<section id=\"shared-1-0\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan <span class=\"badge\">near-term</span></h4><p>The detected primitive is vulnerable to cryptographically relevant quantum attacks. Hybrid rollout minimizes compatibility risk.</p><ol>\n<li>Inventory all call sites using this algorithm and owner teams.</li>\n<li>Check for an existing classical + PQC composition; if migration is needed, evaluate compatible staged or hybrid modes before hard cut-over.</li>\n<li>Define retirement dates for legacy classical algorithms.</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>References and examples</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n</section>\n<section id=\"shared-1-1\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities <span class=\"badge\">planned</span></h4><p>Source declarations and primitive availability do not establish deployment or peer support.</p><ol>\n<li>JDK 24 adds ML-KEM and ML-DSA primitives. Check deployed JSSE hybrid TLS support separately and inspect jdk.tls.namedGroups restrictions.</li>\n<li>Check resolved versions, provider/features and interoperability before changing production policy.</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>References and examples</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/27/security/java-secure-socket-extension-jsse-reference-guide.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/27/security/java-secure-socket-extension-jsse-reference-guide.html</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n</section>\n</details>\n</div></details>\n<details class=\"rule-card\" id=\"rule-2\" data-rule data-page-size=\"20\"><summary><span><strong>Synthetic migration reference</strong> <code>JAVA_UNKNOWN056</code></span><span class=\"sev medium\">medium</span><span class=\"count\">1 hits</span><span>Files 1 / matches <span data-match-count></span></span></summary><div class=\"rule-body\"><p>Review actual use before migration</p>\n<h4>Locations and next steps</h4><nav data-occ-pager hidden><button type=\"button\" data-occ-prev>Previous locations</button><span data-occ-status aria-live=\"polite\"></span><button type=\"button\" data-occ-next>Next locations</button></nav><div data-occurrence-list>\n<details class=\"occurrence\" id=\"finding-2\" data-finding-id=\"JAVA_UNKNOWN056\" data-inventory=\"false\" data-severity=\"medium\" data-risk=\"quantum-vulnerable\" data-search=\"JAVA_UNKNOWN056 Synthetic migration reference unknown/Example.java\"><summary><code>unknown/Example.java:1:1</code><span class=\"occ-match\">synthetic reference</span><span class=\"next-step\">Next: Provide BouncyCastle PQC fallback path</span></summary><p>Risk: quantum-vulnerable</p><p>Check: Review actual use before migration</p><p>Evidence: <code>synthetic reference</code></p>\n<p>Source context unavailable; inspect the original file.</p>\n<h4>Recommended Actions</h4>\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>Check Java runtime baseline for standard PQC APIs <span class=\"badge\">planned</span></h4><p>The Java version is unknown; verify the deployed runtime before selecting a PQC API baseline.</p><ol>\n<li>Target JDK 24+ for ML-KEM an