tography\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"java.jca-ml-dsa-ml-kem\",\n          \"title\": \"Use Java standard JCA names for ML-DSA / ML-KEM\",\n          \"priority\": \"near-term\",\n          \"rationale\": \"Modern JDKs expose standardized PQC algorithm names through JCA, reducing vendor lock-in.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Select an explicit parameter set and generate a new ML-DSA key pair; never reuse RSA key material.\",\n            \"Provision matching public keys and required JOSE/PKI encodings to all verifiers before switching signers to ML-DSA where policy allows.\",\n            \"Adopt ML-KEM for key establishment in hybrid TLS/key exchange designs.\",\n            \"Keep dual verification during migration to preserve compatibility.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://openjdk.org/jeps/496\",\n            \"https://openjdk.org/jeps/497\"\n          ],\n          \"code_examples\": [\n            {\n              \"language\": \"java\",\n              \"before\": \"Signature sig = Signature.getInstance(\\\"SHA256withRSA\\\");\\nsig.initSign(privateKey);\\nsig.update(payload);\\nbyte[] signature = sig.sign();\",\n              \"after\": \"// JDK 24+: provision a new ML-DSA key pair for the selected parameter set.\\n// mlDsaPrivateKey is its private key, never the previous RSA key.\\n// Provision the matching public key and encoding to verifiers before rollout.\\nSignature sig = Signature.getInstance(\\\"ML-DSA\\\");\\nsig.initSign(mlDsaPrivateKey);\\nsig.update(payload);\\nbyte[] signature = sig.sign();\\n// Keep legacy verification only under the explicit migration policy.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"runtime.verify-pqc-capabilities\",\n          \"title\": \"Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities\",\n          \"priority\": \"planned\",\n          \"rationale\": \"Source declarations and primitive availability do not establish deployment or peer support.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"JDK 24 adds ML-KEM and ML-DSA primitives. Check deployed JSSE hybrid TLS support separately and inspect jdk.tls.namedGroups restrictions.\",\n            \"Check resolved versions, provider/features and interoperability before changing production policy.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/27/security/java-secure-socket-extension-jsse-reference-guide.html\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"PKI056\",\n      \"rule_id\": \"PKI056\",\n      \"category\": \"PKI\",\n      \"risk\": \"quantum-vulnerable\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.8,\n      \"description\": \"Synthetic migration reference\",\n      \"migration_hint\": \"Review actual use before migration\",\n      \"location\": {\n        \"file\": \"certificate.pem\",\n        \"line\": 1,\n        \"column\": 1\n      },\n      \"evidence\": {\n        \"type\": \"configuration_match\",\n        \"match\": \"synthetic reference\",\n        \"snippet_preview\": \"synthetic reference\",\n        \"metadata\": {\n          \"scope\": \"config\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"recommended_actions\": [\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"plan.hybrid-migration\",\n          \"title\": \"Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan\",\n          \"priority\": \"near-term\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The detected primitive is vulnerable to cryptographically relevant quantum attacks. Hybrid rollout minimizes compatibility risk.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Inventory all call sites using this algorithm and owner teams.\",\n            \"Check for an existing classical + PQC composition; if migration is needed, evaluate compatible staged or hybrid modes before hard cut-over.\",\n            \"Define retirement dates for legacy classical algorithms.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"pki.hybrid-certificate-roadmap\",\n          \"title\": \"Plan certificate algorithm and trust-store migration\",\n          \"priority\": \"near-term\",\n          \"rationale\": \"PKI updates require coordinated CA, chain, and relying-party compatibility planning. FIPS 204/205 standardize signature primitives, not a universal hybrid certificate format.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Inventory certificate signature algorithms and key sizes from CBOM/report output.\",\n            \"Identify the exact certificate construction and encoding, then verify provider, CA, client and trust-store support before planning issuance.\",\n            \"Pilot only a supported construction in non-production trust stores; if format or ecosystem support is unavailable, keep issuance unverified and evaluate another supported migration path.\",\n            \"Define reissuance plan for quantum-vulnerable roots/intermediates/end-entity certs.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/205/final\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"ENVOY056\",\n      \"rule_id\": \"ENVOY056\",\n      \"category\": \"TLS\",\n      \"risk\": \"quantum-vulnerable\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.8,\n      \"description\": \"Synthetic migration reference\",\n      \"migration_hint\": \"Review actual use before migration\",\n      \"location\": {\n        \"file\": \"envoy.yaml\",\n        \"line\": 1,\n        \"column\": 1\n      },\n      \"evidence\": {\n        \"type\": \"configuration_match\",\n        \"match\": \"synthetic reference\",\n        \"snippet_preview\": \"synthetic reference\",\n        \"metadata\": {\n          \"scope\": \"config\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"recommended_actions\": [\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"envoy.pqc-signature-readiness-note\",\n          \"title\": \"Validate Envoy PQC signature compatibility in control/data planes\",\n          \"priority\": \"advisory\",\n          \"rationale\": \"Envoy TLS behavior depends on configured providers and peer capabilities; PQC signature readiness can vary between mesh edges, sidecars, and external clients.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Harden min/max TLS versions and retire static RSA key exchange where configured; ECDHE_RSA uses RSA authentication, not static RSA key exchange.\",\n            \"Review cipher_suites for TLS 1.0-1.2, not TLS 1.3; review certificate signatures and peer compatibility separately.\",\n            \"Verify PQC certificate-signature compatibility in both downstream and upstream clusters.\",\n            \"Gate production rollout with staged canary tests and explicit fallback paths.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/intro/arch_overview/security/ssl.html\",\n            \"https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"plan.hybrid-migration\",\n          \"title\": \"Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan\",\n          \"priority\": \"near-term\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The detected primitive is vulnerable to cryptographically relevant quantum attacks. Hybrid rollout minimizes compatibility risk.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Inventory all call sites using this algorithm and owner teams.\",\n            \"Check for an existing classical + PQC composition; if migration is needed, evaluate compatible staged or hybrid modes before hard cut-over.\",\n            \"Define retirement dates for legacy classical algorithms.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"tls.remove-rsa-kex\",\n          \"title\": \"Prefer TLS 1.3 and review legacy key exchange\",\n          \"priority\": \"near-term\",\n          \"rationale\": \"RSA key exchange and legacy protocol versions are high-priority migration blockers for PQC readiness.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Prefer TLS 1.3; restrict connections to TLS 1.3 when all peers support it. Disable TLS 1.0 and 1.1.\",\n            \"Retain securely configured TLS 1.2 only where interoperability requires it, and record the compatibility reason.\",\n            \"Prefer ECDHE today and plan hybrid KEM suites for next phase.\",\n            \"Continuously test interoperability across clients and load balancers.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"tls.envoy-hardening\",\n          \"title\": \"Set modern TLS policy in Envoy\",\n          \"priority\": \"near-term\",\n          \"rationale\": \"Envoy control-plane config supports strict min/max protocol and cipher suite policy.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Prefer `tls_minimum_protocol_version: TLSv1_3`; use TLSv1_2 only when interoperability requires it.\",\n            \"Review `cipher_suites` for TLS 1.0-1.2, not TLS 1.3. Retire static RSA key exchange where configured; ECDHE_RSA uses RSA authentication, not static RSA key exchange.\",\n            \"Review certificate-signature migration and peer compatibility separately before removing RSA authentication.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cbom\": [],\n  \"dependency_sbom\": [],\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"total_findings\": 4,\n    \"by_severity\": {\n      \"medium\": 4\n    },\n    \"by_risk\": {\n      \"quantum-vulnerable\": 4\n    },\n    \"scanned_files\": 4,\n    \"skipped_files\": 0\n  }\n}","en/report.md":"# PQC Migration Scan Report\n\nGenerated: 2026-11-15 00:00:00 UTC\n\nRisk candidates: 4 / Inventory findings: 0 / Scanned files: 4\n\nCryptographic references found in source code and configuration.\n\n|Severity|Count (all findings)|\n|---|---:|\n|medium|4|\n\n## Risk candidate index\n\n|Rule / description|Severity|Risk|Hits|Files|\n|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n|[ENVOY056](#rule-0) Synthetic migration reference|medium|quantum-vulnerable|1|1|\n|[JAVA_CURRENT056](#rule-1) Synthetic migration reference|medium|quantum-vulnerable|1|1|\n|[JAVA_UNKNOWN056](#rule-2) Synthetic migration reference|medium|quantum-vulnerable|1|1|\n|[PKI056](#rule-3) Synthetic migration reference|medium|quantum-vulnerable|1|1|\n\n## Informational inventory index\n\n|Rule / description|Severity|Risk|Hits|Files|\n|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n\n<a id=\"rule-0\"></a>\n\n## ENVOY056\n\nSynthetic migration reference\n\nCheck: Review actual use before migration\n\n|Location|Evidence|Next action / details|\n|---|---|---|\n|<a id=\"finding-0\"></a>[envoy.yaml:1:1](#finding-0)|synthetic reference|Prefer TLS 1.3 and review legacy key exchange / [Validate Envoy PQC signature compatibility in control/data planes](#action-0) / [Prefer TLS 1.3 and review legacy key exchange](#action-2) / [Set modern TLS policy in Envoy](#action-3) / Source unavailable|\n\nShared checks for these locations (not verified facts about each line):\n\n- [Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan](#action-1)\n\n<a id=\"rule-1\"></a>\n\n## JAVA_CURRENT056\n\nSynthetic migration reference\n\nCheck: Review actual use before migration\n\n|Location|Evidence|Next action / details|\n|---|---|---|\n|<a id=\"finding-1\"></a>[current/Example.java:1:1](#finding-1)|synthetic reference|Use Java standard JCA names for ML-DSA / ML-KEM / [Use Java standard JCA names for ML-DSA / ML-KEM](#action-4) / Source unavailable|\n\nShared checks for these locations (not verified facts about each line):\n\n- [Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan](#action-1)\n- [Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities](#action-5)\n\n<a id=\"rule-2\"></a>\n\n## JAVA_UNKNOWN056\n\nSynthetic migration reference\n\nCheck: Review actual use before migration\n\n|Location|Evidence|Next action / details|\n|---|---|---|\n|<a id=\"finding-2\"></a>[unknown/Example.java:1:1](#finding-2)|synthetic reference|Provide BouncyCastle PQC fallback path / [Check Java runtime baseline for standard PQC APIs](#action-6) / [Provide BouncyCastle PQC fallback path](#action-7) / Source unavailable|\n\nShared checks for these locations (not verified facts about each line):\n\n- [Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan](#action-1)\n- [Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities](#action-5)\n\n<a id=\"rule-3\"></a>\n\n## PKI056\n\nSynthetic migration reference\n\nCheck: Review actual use before migration\n\n|Location|Evidence|Next action / details|\n|---|---|---|\n|<a id=\"finding-3\"></a>[certificate.pem:1:1](#finding-3)|synthetic reference|Review actual use before migration / Source unavailable|\n\nShared checks for these locations (not verified facts about each line):\n\n- [Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan](#action-1)\n- [Plan certificate algorithm and trust-store migration](#action-8)\n\n## Action details\n\nEach location links only to its applicable action. Identical payloads are printed once.\n\n<a id=\"action-0\"></a>\n\n\n#### Validate Envoy PQC signature compatibility in control/data planes (advisory)\n\nEnvoy TLS behavior depends on configured providers and peer capabilities; PQC signature readiness can vary between mesh edges, sidecars, and external clients.\n\n1. Harden min/max TLS versions and retire static RSA key exchange where configured; ECDHE_RSA uses RSA authentication, not static RSA key exchange.\n2. Review cipher_suites for TLS 1.0-1.2, not TLS 1.3; review certificate signatures and peer compatibility separately.\n3. Verify PQC certificate-signature compatibility in both downstream and upstream clusters.\n4. Gate production rollout with staged canary tests and explicit fallback paths.\n\nReferences:\n\n- https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/intro/arch_overview/security/ssl.html\n- https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto\n<a id=\"action-1\"></a>\n\n\n#### Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term)\n\nThe detected primitive is vulnerable to cryptographically relevant quantum attacks. Hybrid rollout minimizes compatibility risk.\n\n1. Inventory all call sites using this algorithm and owner teams.\n2. Check for an existing classical + PQC composition; if migration is needed, evaluate compatible staged or hybrid modes before hard cut-over.\n3. Define retirement dates for legacy classical algorithms.\n\nReferences:\n\n- https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography\n- https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final\n- https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\n<a id=\"action-2\"></a>\n\n\n#### Prefer TLS 1.3 and review legacy key exchange (near-term)\n\nRSA key exchange and legacy protocol versions are high-priority migration blockers for PQC readiness.\n\n1. Prefer TLS 1.3; restrict connections to TLS 1.3 when all peers support it. Disable TLS 1.0 and 1.1.\n2. Retain securely configured TLS 1.2 only where interoperability requires it, and record the compatibility reason.\n3. Prefer ECDHE today and plan hybrid KEM suites for next phase.\n4. Continuously test interoperability across clients and load balancers.\n\nReferences:\n\n- https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446\n<a id=\"action-3\"></a>\n\n\n#### Set modern TLS policy in Envoy (near-term)\n\nEnvoy control-plane config supports strict min/max protocol and cipher suite policy.\n\n1. Prefer \\`tls_minimum_protocol_version: TLSv1_3\\`; use TLSv1_2 only when interoperability requires it.\n2. Review \\`cipher_suites\\` for TLS 1.0-1.2, not TLS 1.3. Retire static RSA key exchange where configured; ECDHE_RSA uses RSA authentication, not static RSA key exchange.\n3. Review certificate-signature migration and peer compatibility separately before removing RSA authentication.\n\nReferences:\n\n- https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto\n<a id=\"action-4\"></a>\n\n\n#### Use Java standard JCA names for ML-DSA / ML-KEM (near-term)\n\nModern JDKs expose standardized PQC algorithm names through JCA, reducing vendor lock-in.\n\n1. Select an explicit parameter set and generate a new ML-DSA key pair; never reuse RSA key material.\n2. Provision matching public keys and required JOSE/PKI encodings to all verifiers before switching signers to ML-DSA where policy allows.\n3. Adopt ML-KEM for key establishment in hybrid TLS/key exchange designs.\n4. Keep dual verification during migration to preserve compatibility.\n\nReferences:\n\n- https://openjdk.org/jeps/496\n- https://openjdk.org/jeps/497\n\nBefore (java)\n\n    Signature sig = Signature.getInstance(\"SHA256withRSA\");\n    sig.initSign(privateKey);\n    sig.update(payload);\n    byte[] signature = sig.sign();\n\nAfter\n\n    // JDK 24+: provision a new ML-DSA key pair for the selected parameter set.\n    // mlDsaPrivateKey is its private key, never the previous RSA key.\n    // Provision the matching public key and encoding to verifiers before rollout.\n    Signature sig = Signature.getInstance(\"ML-DSA\");\n    sig.initSign(mlDsaPrivateKey);\n    sig.update(payload);\n    byte[] signature = sig.sign();\n    // Keep legacy verification only under the explicit migration policy.\n\n<a id=\"action-5\"></a>\n\n\n#### Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities (planned)\n\nSource declarations and primitive availability do not establish deployment or peer support.\n\n1. JDK 24 adds ML-KEM and ML-DSA primitives. Check deployed JSSE hybrid TLS support separately and inspect jdk.tls.namedGroups restrictions.\n2. Check resolved versions, provider/features and interoperability before changing production policy.\n\nReferences:\n\n- https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/27/security/java-secure-socket-extension-jsse-reference-guide.html\n<a id=\"action-6\"></a>\n\n\n#### Check Java runtime baseline for standard PQC APIs (planned)\n\nThe Java version is unknown; verify the deployed runtime before selecting a PQC API baseline.\n\n1. Target JDK 24+ for ML-KEM and ML-DSA support planning.\n2. Pilot compatibility testing in CI before production migration.\n\nReferences:\n\n- https://openjdk.org/jeps/496\n- https://openjdk.org/jeps/497\n<a id=\"action-7\"></a>\n\n\n#### Provide BouncyCastle PQC fallback path (near-term)\n\nBouncyCastle can be used as a pragmatic transition option when standard runtime support is unavailable or incomplete.\n\n1. Verify the resolved BC release and deployed JDK support before provider initialization; the example uses BC Java 1.85 and the BC provider, not BCPQC.\n2. Select explicit ML-DSA / ML-KEM parameter sets for the intended purpose. Generate new algorithm-compatible keys and provision matching public keys and encodings to verifiers; never reuse RSA key material.\n3. Document provider ordering and FIPS/compliance impact.\n\nReferences:\n\n- https://www.bouncycastle.org/java.html\n- https://downloads.bouncycastle.org/java/docs/bcprov-jdk18on-javadoc/\n\nBefore (java)\n\n    Security.addProvider(new BouncyCastleProvider());\n    Signature sig = Signature.getInstance(\"SHA256withRSA\", \"BC\");\n\nAfter\n\n    // BC Java 1.85 example: verify the resolved release/provider supports this name.\n    Security.addProvider(new BouncyCastleProvider());\n    // Provision a new ML-DSA-65 key pair and its public key to verifiers.\n    // mlDsaPrivateKey must not be the previous RSA key.\n    Signature sig = Signature.getInstance(\"ML-DSA-65\", \"BC\");\n    sig.initSign(mlDsaPrivateKey);\n\n<a id=\"action-8\"></a>\n\n\n#### Plan certificate algorithm and trust-store migration (near-term)\n\nPKI updates require coordinated CA, chain, and relying-party compatibility planning. FIPS 204/205 standardize signature primitives, not a universal hybrid certificate format.\n\n1. Inventory certificate signature algorithms and key sizes from CBOM/report output.\n2. Identify the exact certificate construction and encoding, then verify provider, CA, client and trust-store support before planning issuance.\n3. Pilot only a supported construction in non-production trust stores; if format or ecosystem support is unavailable, keep issuance unverified and evaluate another supported migration path.\n4. Define reissuance plan for quantum-vulnerable roots/intermediates/end-entity certs.\n\nReferences:\n\n- https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\n- https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/205/final\n\n## Inventory exports\n\n- [CBOM](cbom.json): 0\n- [Dependency SBOM](dependency-sbom.json): 0\n\n","en/report.sarif":"{\n  \"version\": \"2.1.0\",\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json\",\n  \"runs\": [\n    {\n      \"columnKind\": \"unicodeCodePoints\",\n      \"tool\": {\n        \"driver\": {\n          \"name\": \"pqc-scan\",\n          \"rules\": [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"ENVOY056\",\n              \"shortDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"TLS\"\n              },\n              \"fullDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference\"\n              },\n              \"defaultConfiguration\": {\n                \"level\": \"warning\"\n              }\n            },\n            {\n              \"id\": \"JAVA_CURRENT056\",\n              \"shortDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"CryptoAPI\"\n              },\n              \"fullDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference\"\n              },\n              \"defaultConfiguration\": {\n                \"level\": \"warning\"\n              }\n            },\n            {\n              \"id\": \"JAVA_UNKNOWN056\",\n              \"shortDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"CryptoAPI\"\n              },\n              \"fullDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference\"\n              },\n              \"defaultConfiguration\": {\n                \"level\": \"warning\"\n              }\n            },\n            {\n              \"id\": \"PKI056\",\n              \"shortDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"PKI\"\n              },\n              \"fullDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference\"\n              },\n              \"defaultConfiguration\": {\n                \"level\": \"warning\"\n              }\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      },\n      \"results\": [\n        {\n          \"ruleId\": \"JAVA_UNKNOWN056\",\n          \"level\": \"warning\",\n          \"message\": {\n            \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference | migration_hint=Review actual use before migration | next_actions=Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term); Check Java runtime baseline for standard PQC APIs (planned); Provide BouncyCastle PQC fallback path (near-term); Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities (planned)\"\n          },\n          \"locations\": [\n            {\n              \"physicalLocation\": {\n                \"artifactLocation\": {\n                  \"uri\": \"unknown/Example.java\"\n                },\n                \"region\": {\n                  \"startLine\": 1,\n                  \"startColumn\": 1\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          ],\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"migration_hint\": \"Review actual use before migration\",\n            \"recommended_actions\": [\n              \"Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term)\",\n              \"Check Java runtime baseline for standard PQC APIs (planned)\",\n              \"Provide BouncyCastle PQC fallback path (near-term)\",\n              \"Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities (planned)\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"ruleId\": \"JAVA_CURRENT056\",\n          \"level\": \"warning\",\n          \"message\": {\n            \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference | migration_hint=Review actual use before migration | next_actions=Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term); Use Java standard JCA names for ML-DSA / ML-KEM (near-term); Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities (planned)\"\n          },\n          \"locations\": [\n            {\n              \"physicalLocation\": {\n                \"artifactLocation\": {\n                  \"uri\": \"current/Example.java\"\n                },\n                \"region\": {\n                  \"startLine\": 1,\n                  \"startColumn\": 1\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          ],\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"migration_hint\": \"Review actual use before migration\",\n            \"recommended_actions\": [\n              \"Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term)\",\n              \"Use Java standard JCA names for ML-DSA / ML-KEM (near-term)\",\n              \"Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities (planned)\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"ruleId\": \"PKI056\",\n          \"level\": \"warning\",\n          \"message\": {\n            \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference | migration_hint=Review actual use before migration | next_actions=Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term); Plan certificate algorithm and trust-store migration (near-term)\"\n          },\n          \"locations\": [\n            {\n              \"physicalLocation\": {\n                \"artifactLocation\": {\n                  \"uri\": \"certificate.pem\"\n                },\n                \"region\": {\n                  \"startLine\": 1,\n                  \"startColumn\": 1\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          ],\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"migration_hint\": \"Review actual use before migration\",\n            \"recommended_actions\": [\n              \"Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term)\",\n              \"Plan certificate algorithm and trust-store migration (near-term)\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"ruleId\": \"ENVOY056\",\n          \"level\": \"warning\",\n          \"message\": {\n            \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference | migration_hint=Review actual use before migration | next_actions=Validate Envoy PQC signature compatibility in control/data planes (advisory); Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term); Prefer TLS 1.3 and review legacy key exchange (near-term); Set modern TLS policy in Envoy (near-term)\"\n          },\n          \"locations\": [\n            {\n              \"physicalLocation\": {\n                \"artifactLocation\": {\n                  \"uri\": \"envoy.yaml\"\n                },\n                \"region\": {\n                  \"startLine\": 1,\n                  \"startColumn\": 1\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          ],\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"migration_hint\": \"Review actual use before migration\",\n            \"recommended_actions\": [\n              \"Validate Envoy PQC signature compatibility in control/data planes (advisory)\",\n              \"Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term)\",\n              \"Prefer TLS 1.3 and review legacy key exchange (near-term)\",\n              \"Set modern TLS policy in Envoy (near-term)\"\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}","ja/report.html":"<!doctype html><html lang=\"ja\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\"><title>耐量子暗号への移行調査レポート</title><style>\n:root {\n  --bg: #f5f7fb;\n  --card: #ffffff;\n  --text: #1a2233;\n  --muted: #5e6b85;\n  --border: #dfe5f2;\n  --hl: #fff2c7;\n  --line: #f8fafc;\n  --critical: #9d0208;\n  --high: #d00000;\n  --medium: #ef8a17;\n  --low: #1f7a8c;\n  --info: #3d5a80;\n}\n* { box-sizing: border-box; }\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-family: \"IBM Plex Sans\", \"Noto Sans\", sans-serif;\n  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #eef3fb 0%, var(--bg) 100%);\n  color: var(--text);\n}\n.container {\n  width: min(1200px, 96vw);\n  margin: 0 auto;\n  padding: 20px 12px 40px;\n}\n.top h1 { margin: 0; font-size: 28px; }\n.meta { color: var(--muted); margin-top: 8px; }\n.summary {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr));\n  gap: 12px;\n  margin: 18px 0 22px;\n}\n.metric {\n  background: var(--card);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius: 10px;\n  padding: 12px;\n}\n.metric-label { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }\n.metric-value { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 700; }\n.finding {\n  background: var(--card);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius: 12px;\n  padding: 14px;\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\n}\n.finding h3 {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-size: 18px;\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 10px;\n  align-items: center;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n}\n.desc {\n  margin: 10px 0 10px;\n  color: #26324a;\n}\n.kv {\n  margin: 0 0 10px;\n  padding-left: 18px;\n}\n.kv li {\n  margin: 4px 0;\n}\n.sev {\n  font-size: 12px;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  padding: 3px 9px;\n  border: 1px solid transparent;\n}\n.sev.critical { background: #ffe5e8; color: var(--critical); border-color: #f3b8bf; }\n.sev.high { background: #ffe9e9; color: var(--high); border-color: #f7c0c0; }\n.sev.medium { background: #fff4df; color: var(--medium); border-color: #f7d7a2; }\n.sev.low { background: #e5f5f8; color: var(--low); border-color: #b8dde4; }\n.sev.info { background: #e7eef7; color: var(--info); border-color: #c7d6ea; }\n.count {\n  font-size: 12px;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  border: 1px solid #d6dfef;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  padding: 2px 8px;\n  background: #f7f9fe;\n}\n.snippet-wrap {\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  margin-bottom: 10px;\n}\n.evidence-list {\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  margin-bottom: 10px;\n  background: #fbfcff;\n}\n.occurrence-wrap {\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  margin-bottom: 10px;\n  background: #fbfcff;\n}\n.occurrence-scroll {\n  width: 100%;\n  overflow-x: auto;\n}\n.snippet-title {\n  background: #f3f6fc;\n  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\n  padding: 6px 10px;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  color: var(--muted);\n}\n.code-lines {\n  background: #fbfcff;\n  font-family: \"JetBrains Mono\", \"SFMono-Regular\", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;\n  font-size: 13px;\n  line-height: 1.2;\n}\npre {\n  margin: 0;\n  overflow-x: auto;\n  background: #fbfcff;\n}\ncode {\n  display: inline;\n  font-family: \"JetBrains Mono\", \"SFMono-Regular\", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;\n  font-size: 12.5px;\n  line-height: 1.35;\n}\npre code {\n  display: block;\n  font-size: 13px;\n  line-height: 1.28;\n}\n.occ-table {\n  width: 100%;\n  table-layout: fixed;\n  border-collapse: collapse;\n  font-size: 13px;\n}\n.occ-table th, .occ-table td {\n  border-top: 1px solid #e4ebf7;\n  padding: 6px 8px;\n  text-align: left;\n  vertical-align: top;\n}\n.occ-table th {\n  background: #f8faff;\n  color: #3b4964;\n  font-weight: 600;\n}\n.occ-table th:nth-child(1),\n.occ-table td:nth-child(1) {\n  width: 54%;\n}\n.occ-table td:nth-child(2) {\n  width: 72px;\n  text-align: right;\n}\n.occ-table th:nth-child(3),\n.occ-table td:nth-child(3) {\n  width: 20%;\n}\n.occ-table th:nth-child(4),\n.occ-table td:nth-child(4) {\n  width: 20%;\n}\n.file-toggle {\n  border: 0;\n  background: transparent;\n  color: #1b5fbf;\n  text-decoration: underline;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  padding: 0;\n  width: 100%;\n  text-align: left;\n  white-space: normal;\n  overflow-wrap: anywhere;\n  word-break: break-word;\n}\n.file-toggle code {\n  color: inherit;\n  white-space: normal;\n  overflow-wrap: anywhere;\n  word-break: break-word;\n}\n.occ-table td code {\n  white-space: normal;\n  overflow-wrap: anywhere;\n  word-break: break-word;\n}\n.line {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 56px 1fr;\n  column-gap: 8px;\n  background: var(--line);\n  min-height: 1.5em;\n}\n.line.hl {\n  background: var(--hl);\n}\n.ln {\n  user-select: none;\n  text-align: right;\n  color: #73819c;\n  border-right: 1px solid #dfe5f2;\n  padding: 0 8px 0 0;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n.tx {\n  white-space: pre;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n.occ-snippet-row.hidden {\n  display: none;\n}\n.occ-snippet-inline {\n  background: #f9fbff;\n  border: 1px solid #e2e9f7;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  padding: 8px;\n}\n.occ-snippet-inline .snippet-wrap {\n  margin-top: 8px;\n}\n.actions {\n  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);\n  padding-top: 8px;\n}\n.actions h4 { margin: 0 0 8px; }\n.action {\n  border: 1px dashed #d7deed;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  padding: 8px 10px;\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\n  background: #fafcff;\n}\n.action-title {\n  font-weight: 600;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 8px;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n}\n.badge {\n  font-size: 11px;\n  border: 1px solid #bfcbe3;\n  background: #edf2fb;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  padding: 2px 8px;\n}\n.refs {\n  margin: 6px 0;\n  padding-left: 18px;\n}\n.code-example {\n  margin-top: 6px;\n}\n.code-label {\n  color: var(--muted);\n  font-size: 12px;\n  margin-bottom: 3px;\n}\n@media (max-width: 640px) {\n  .line { grid-template-columns: 46px 1fr; }\n  code { font-size: 12px; }\n  .occ-table th:nth-child(1),\n  .occ-table td:nth-child(1) {\n    width: 48%;\n  }\n}\n\n[hidden] { display: none !important; }\n[data-report-controls] { display:flex; gap:12px; flex-wrap:wrap; padding:16px; border:1px solid var(--line, #ced8de); border-radius:12px; margin:18px 0; }\n[data-report-controls] label { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:5px; }\ninput, select, button { font:inherit; padding:7px 10px; max-width:100%; }\nbutton { cursor:pointer; }\nbutton:disabled { cursor:default; opacity:.5; }\nnav { display:flex; align-items:center; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:12px; margin:14px 0; }\nsummary { cursor:pointer; padding:14px; overflow-wrap:anywhere; }\nsummary:focus-visible, button:focus-visible, a:focus-visible, input:focus-visible, select:focus-visible { outline:3px solid #087f8c; outline-offset:3px; }\n.rule-card { border:1px solid #b9cbd2; border-radius:12px; margin:12px 0; background:#ffffffd9; }\n.rule-card > summary { display:list-item; }\n.rule-card > summary > span { margin-right:12px; }\n.rule-body { padding:0 18px 18px; }\n.occurrence { border-top:1px solid #dce4e8; padding-bottom:8px; }\n.occurrence > :not(summary) { margin-left:16px; margin-right:16px; }\n.occ-match { display:block; color:#576975; font-size:.9em; }\n.next-step { display:block; padding-top:5px; }\n.action { border-left:3px solid #087f8c; padding:4px 14px; margin:14px 0; }\n.shared { margin-top:16px; background:#f2f6f7; border-radius:8px; }\npre { overflow:auto; padding:12px; background:#eef2f4; }\ncode, .tx { overflow-wrap:anywhere; }\n@media (max-width:640px) { .rule-body { padding:0 8px 10px; } .rule-card > summary > span { display:block; margin:4px 0; } [data-report-controls] label { width:100%; } .occurrence > :not(summary) { margin-left:8px; margin-right:8px; } }\n/* Inventory identifiers must fit narrow screens without altering their values. */\n.inspection-context table { width: 100%; table-layout: fixed; }\n.inspection-context th, .inspection-context td { overflow-wrap: anywhere; word-break: break-word; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }\n\n.inspection-overview { border:1px solid #b9cbd2; border-left:5px solid #087f8c; border-radius:12px; padding:18px; margin:20px 0; background:#f3f8f9; overflow-wrap:anywhere; }\n.inspection-status { font-size:1.15rem; font-weight:700; }\n.inspection-metrics { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:12px; }\n.inspection-metrics > div { background:#fff; border:1px solid #dce4e8; border-radius:8px; padding:12px; }\n.inspection-metrics strong { display:block; font-size:1.7rem; }\n.inspection-scope { padding-left:22px; }\n.inspection-reasons { border-top:1px solid #ced8de; margin-top:14px; }\n.inspection-reason { border-top:1px solid #dce4e8; padding:4px 12px; }\n@media (max-width:640px) { .inspection-metrics { grid-template-columns:1fr; } .inspection-overview { padding:12px; } }\n</style></head><body><main class=\"container\" data-compact-report>\n<header class=\"top\"><h1>耐量子暗号への移行調査レポート</h1><p class=\"meta\">作成日時: 2026-11-15 00:00:00 UTC</p><p>コードや設定の手掛かりをまとめた調査結果です。</p></header>\n<section class=\"summary\">\n<div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric-label\">対応を確認する候補</div><div class=\"metric-value\">4</div></div>\n<div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric-label\">参考情報</div><div class=\"metric-value\">0</div></div>\n<div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric-label\">調査したファイル</div><div class=\"metric-value\">4</div></div>\n<div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric-label\">対象外のファイル</div><div class=\"metric-value\">0</div></div>\n<div class=\"metric\"><div class=\"metric-label\">該当ファイル</div><div class=\"metric-value\">4</div></div>\n</section>\n<p>重大度の内訳（全検出）：</p><p>\n<span class=\"sev medium\">中: 4</span> </p>\n<section data-report-controls hidden aria-label=\"表示の絞り込み\"><label>表示対象<select data-mode><option value=\"candidate\">対応候補</option><option value=\"inventory\">参考情報</option><option value=\"all\">すべて</option></select></label><label>検索<input data-search type=\"search\" placeholder=\"ルール・説明・ファイル名\"></label><label>重大度<select data-severity><option value=\"\">すべて</option>\n<option value=\"critical\">緊急</option>\n<option value=\"high\">高</option>\n<option value=\"medium\">中</option>\n<option value=\"low\">低</option>\n<option value=\"info\">参考情報</option>\n</select></label><label>リスク<select data-risk><option value=\"\">すべて</option>\n<option value=\"quantum-vulnerable\">量子計算によるリスクあり</option>\n<option value=\"quantum-uncertain\">要確認（実装や設定の確認が必要）</option>\n<option value=\"quantum-safe\">PQC方式の参照あり（対応完了の保証ではありません）</option>\n<option value=\"non-quantum-risk\">量子計算とは別のセキュリティ上の注意点</option>\n</select></label><button type=\"button\" data-reset>条件を解除</button></section><noscript><p>JavaScriptを使わない場合は、全件を表示します。折りたたみは開けますが、検索・絞り込み・ページ切替は使えません。</p></noscript><p data-report-status role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p><p data-empty hidden>表示条件に一致する検出はありません。表示対象や絞り込み条件を変更してください。調査全体で検出がなかったという意味ではありません。</p><nav data-group-pager hidden aria-label=\"ルール一覧のページ\"><button type=\"button\" data-prev>前へ</button><span data-page></span><button type=\"button\" data-next>次へ</button></nav>\n<details class=\"rule-card\" id=\"rule-0\" data-rule data-page-size=\"20\"><summary><span><strong>日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference</strong> <code>ENVOY056</code></span><span class=\"sev medium\">中</span><span class=\"count\">1 件</span><span>ファイル 1 / 表示対象 <span data-match-count></span></span></summary><div class=\"rule-body\"><p>ルール作成者の確認事項（原文）：Review actual use before migration</p>\n<h4>検出箇所と対応</h4><nav data-occ-pager hidden><button type=\"button\" data-occ-prev>前の箇所</button><span data-occ-status aria-live=\"polite\"></span><button type=\"button\" data-occ-next>次の箇所</button></nav><div data-occurrence-list>\n<details class=\"occurrence\" id=\"finding-0\" data-finding-id=\"ENVOY056\" data-inventory=\"false\" data-severity=\"medium\" data-risk=\"quantum-vulnerable\" data-search=\"ENVOY056 日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference envoy.yaml\"><summary><code>envoy.yaml:1:1</code><span class=\"occ-match\">synthetic reference</span><span class=\"next-step\">対応: TLS 1.3を優先し、鍵共有方式を確認する</span></summary><p>判断の目安: 量子計算によるリスクあり</p><p>確認すること: ルール作成者の確認事項（原文）：Review actual use before migration</p><p>検出した記述: <code>synthetic reference</code></p>\n<p>周辺のコードは取得できませんでした。元のファイルを確認してください。</p>\n<h4>この箇所の対応</h4>\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>EnvoyのPQC証明書署名の互換性を確認する <span class=\"badge\">advisory</span></h4><p>鍵共有と証明書の署名は別です。プロバイダーと通信相手の対応を確認してください。</p><ol>\n<li>TLSの最低・最高バージョンを見直し、設定に静的RSA鍵交換があれば移行を検討してください。ECDHE_RSAのRSA認証とは区別してください。</li>\n<li>cipher_suitesはTLS 1.0〜1.2の設定で、TLS 1.3には適用されません。</li>\n<li>下流・上流の両方でPQC証明書署名の互換性を試し、段階的な展開と切戻しを準備してください。</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>参考資料・変更例</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/intro/arch_overview/security/ssl.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/intro/arch_overview/security/ssl.html</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>TLS 1.3を優先し、鍵共有方式を確認する <span class=\"badge\">早めに対応</span></h4><p>RSA鍵交換や古いTLS設定は移行時の確認対象です。この一般的な確認項目だけで、RSAの利用が確定するわけではありません。</p><ol>\n<li>TLS 1.3を優先し、全接続先が対応していれば1.3だけを許可してください。TLS 1.0・1.1は無効にしてください。</li>\n<li>TLS 1.2は互換性が必要な場合に限り、安全な設定で残してください。理由を記録し、鍵共有方式のPQC対応も別に確認してください。</li>\n<li>クライアントと負荷分散装置を含め、互換性を継続して確認してください。</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>参考資料・変更例</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>EnvoyのTLS設定を見直す <span class=\"badge\">早めに対応</span></h4><p>最低・最高バージョンと暗号スイートを設定で管理できます。</p><ol>\n<li>tls_minimum_protocol_versionはTLSv1_3を優先し、TLSv1_2は互換性が必要な場合に限って検討してください。</li>\n<li>cipher_suitesはTLS 1.0〜1.2の設定で、TLS 1.3には適用されません。静的RSA鍵交換と、ECDHE_RSAのRSA認証を区別してください。</li>\n<li>RSA認証を外す前に、証明書の署名方式と通信相手の互換性を別に確認してください。</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>参考資料・変更例</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n<p>共通の確認・計画（この行で確認済みの事実ではありません）：</p><ul>\n<li><a href=\"#shared-0-0\">既存方式とPQCを併用し、段階的に移行する</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n</div>\n<details class=\"shared\"><summary>共通の確認・計画 (1)</summary>\n<section id=\"shared-0-0\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>既存方式とPQCを併用し、段階的に移行する <span class=\"badge\">早めに対応</span></h4><p>検出した方式には、量子計算による将来のリスクがあります。接続相手との互換性を確かめながら移行を進めてください。</p><ol>\n<li>利用箇所と担当チームを洗い出してください。</li>\n<li>既存のPQC・複合構成を確認し、移行が必要なら新旧方式の併用を試してください。</li>\n<li>旧方式を廃止する条件と時期を決めてください。</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>参考資料・変更例</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n</section>\n</details>\n</div></details>\n<details class=\"rule-card\" id=\"rule-1\" data-rule data-page-size=\"20\"><summary><span><strong>日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference</strong> <code>JAVA_CURRENT056</code></span><span class=\"sev medium\">中</span><span class=\"count\">1 件</span><span>ファイル 1 / 表示対象 <span data-match-count></span></span></summary><div class=\"rule-body\"><p>ルール作成者の確認事項（原文）：Review actual use before migration</p>\n<h4>検出箇所と対応</h4><nav data-occ-pager hidden><button type=\"button\" data-occ-prev>前の箇所</button><span data-occ-status aria-live=\"polite\"></span><button type=\"button\" data-occ-next>次の箇所</button></nav><div data-occurrence-list>\n<details class=\"occurrence\" id=\"finding-1\" data-finding-id=\"JAVA_CURRENT056\" data-inventory=\"false\" data-severity=\"medium\" data-risk=\"quantum-vulnerable\" data-search=\"JAVA_CURRENT056 日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference current/Example.java\"><summary><code>current/Example.java:1:1</code><span class=\"occ-match\">synthetic reference</span><span class=\"next-step\">対応: Java標準のPQC APIへの移行を検討する</span></summary><p>判断の目安: 量子計算によるリスクあり</p><p>確認すること: ルール作成者の確認事項（原文）：Review actual use before migration</p><p>検出した記述: <code>synthetic reference</code></p>\n<p>周辺のコードは取得できませんでした。元のファイルを確認してください。</p>\n<h4>この箇所の対応</h4>\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>Java標準のPQC APIへの移行を検討する <span class=\"badge\">早めに対応</span></h4><p>対応するJDKでは、JCAの標準方式名でML-DSA・ML-KEMを指定できます。</p><ol>\n<li>パラメーターセットを選び、新しいML-DSA鍵ペアを生成してください。RSAの鍵を流用しないでください。</li>\n<li>署名側を切り替える前に、対応する公開鍵とJOSE・PKIの符号化形式をすべての検証側へ配備してください。</li>\n<li>ML-KEMは鍵共有に使う方式です。TLSなどの対応は別に確認してください。</li>\n<li>旧方式の検証を残す条件と廃止時期は、移行方針として明示してください。</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>参考資料・変更例</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://openjdk.org/jeps/496\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://openjdk.org/jeps/496</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://openjdk.org/jeps/497\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://openjdk.org/jeps/497</a></p>\n<p>変更前 (java)</p><pre><code>Signature sig = Signature.getInstance(&quot;SHA256withRSA&quot;);\nsig.initSign(privateKey);\nsig.update(payload);\nbyte[] signature = sig.sign();</code></pre><p>変更後</p><pre><code>// JDK 24+: provision a new ML-DSA key pair for the selected parameter set.\n// mlDsaPrivateKey is its private key, never the previous RSA key.\n// Provision the matching public key and encoding to verifiers before rollout.\nSignature sig = Signature.getInstance(&quot;ML-DSA&quot;);\nsig.initSign(mlDsaPrivateKey);\nsig.update(payload);\nbyte[] signature = sig.sign();\n// Keep legacy verification only under the explicit migration policy.</code></pre>\n</details>\n</section>\n<p>共通の確認・計画（この行で確認済みの事実ではありません）：</p><ul>\n<li><a href=\"#shared-1-0\">既存方式とPQCを併用し、段階的に移行する</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#shared-1-1\">実行環境と通信相手のPQC対応を確認する</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n</div>\n<details class=\"shared\"><summary>共通の確認・計画 (2)</summary>\n<section id=\"shared-1-0\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>既存方式とPQCを併用し、段階的に移行する <span class=\"badge\">早めに対応</span></h4><p>検出した方式には、量子計算による将来のリスクがあります。接続相手との互換性を確かめながら移行を進めてください。</p><ol>\n<li>利用箇所と担当チームを洗い出してください。</li>\n<li>既存のPQC・複合構成を確認し、移行が必要なら新旧方式の併用を試してください。</li>\n<li>旧方式を廃止する条件と時期を決めてください。</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>参考資料・変更例</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n</section>\n<section id=\"shared-1-1\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>実行環境と通信相手のPQC対応を確認する <span class=\"badge\">計画して対応</span></h4><p>コードに方式名があるだけでは、その環境で動くか、接続相手が対応しているかは分かりません。</p><ol>\n<li>JDK 24以降のML-KEM・ML-DSA対応を確認してください。プロバイダーや通信規約の対応は別に確認が必要です。</li>\n<li>実際に配備している版、プロバイダー、機能設定を確認してください。</li>\n<li>本番設定を変える前に、接続相手との互換性を試してください。</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>参考資料・変更例</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/27/security/java-secure-socket-extension-jsse-reference-guide.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/27/security/java-secure-socket-extension-jsse-reference-guide.html</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n</section>\n</details>\n</div></details>\n<details class=\"rule-card\" id=\"rule-2\" data-rule data-page-size=\"20\"><summary><span><strong>日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference</strong> <code>JAVA_UNKNOWN056</code></span><span class=\"sev medium\">中</span><span class=\"count\">1 件</span><span>ファイル 1 / 表示対象 <span data-match-count></span></span></summary><div class=\"rule-body\"><p>ルール作成者の確認事項（原文）：Review actual use before migration</p>\n<h4>検出箇所と対応</h4><nav data-occ-pager hidden><button type=\"button\" data-occ-prev>前の箇所</button><span data-occ-status aria-live=\"polite\"></span><button type=\"button\" data-occ-next>次の箇所</button></nav><div data-occurrence-list>\n<details class=\"occurrence\" id=\"finding-2\" data-finding-id=\"JAVA_UNKNOWN056\" data-inventory=\"false\" data-severity=\"medium\" data-risk=\"quantum-vulnerable\" data-search=\"JAVA_UNKNOWN056 日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference unknown/Example.java\"><summary><code>unknown/Example.java:1:1</code><span class=\"occ-match\">synthetic reference</span><span class=\"next-step\">対応: BouncyCastleによるPQC対応を検討する</span></summary><p>判断の目安: 量子計算によるリスクあり</p><p>確認すること: ルール作成者の確認事項（原文）：Review actual use before migration</p><p>検出した記述: <code>synthetic reference</code></p>\n<p>周辺のコードは取得できませんでした。元のファイルを確認してください。</p>\n<h4>この箇所の対応</h4>\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>Javaの版を確認し、必要ならPQC API対応版へ更新する <span class=\"badge\">計画して対応</span></h4><p>版が不明な場合は、配備先のJavaを確認してください。宣言された版だけでは実環境のAPI対応は確定しません。</p><ol>\n<li>標準のML-KEM・ML-DSA APIが必要な場合は、JDK 24以降の対応を確認してください。</li>\n<li>本番への適用前にCIで互換性を試してください。</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>参考資料・変更例</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://openjdk.org/jeps/496\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://openjdk.org/jeps/496</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://openjdk.org/jeps/497\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://openjdk.org/jeps/497</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>BouncyCastleによるPQC対応を検討する <span class=\"badge\">早めに対応</span></h4><p>標準APIを使えない環境では、ライブラリによる対応が移行候補になります。</p><ol>\n<li>解決済みのBouncyCastleの版と配備先JDKの対応を確認してください。例はBC Java 1.85のBCプロバイダーを使います。BCPQCとは区別してください。</li>\n<li>用途に合うパラメーターセットを選び、新しいML-DSA鍵ペアなど、方式に対応した鍵を生成してください。RSA鍵を流用せず、公開鍵と符号化形式を検証側へ配備してください。</li>\n<li>プロバイダーの優先順位とFIPSなどの運用要件への影響を記録してください。</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>参考資料・変更例</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.bouncycastle.org/java.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.bouncycastle.org/java.html</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://downloads.bouncycastle.org/java/docs/bcprov-jdk18on-javadoc/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://downloads.bouncycastle.org/java/docs/bcprov-jdk18on-javadoc/</a></p>\n<p>変更前 (java)</p><pre><code>Security.addProvider(new BouncyCastleProvider());\nSignature sig = Signature.getInstance(&quot;SHA256withRSA&quot;, &quot;BC&quot;);</code></pre><p>変更後</p><pre><code>// BC Java 1.85 example: verify the resolved release/provider supports this name.\nSecurity.addProvider(new BouncyCastleProvider());\n// Provision a new ML-DSA-65 key pair and its public key to verifiers.\n// mlDsaPrivateKey must not be the previous RSA key.\nSignature sig = Signature.getInstance(&quot;ML-DSA-65&quot;, &quot;BC&quot;);\nsig.initSign(mlDsaPrivateKey);</code></pre>\n</details>\n</section>\n<p>共通の確認・計画（この行で確認済みの事実ではありません）：</p><ul>\n<li><a href=\"#shared-2-0\">既存方式とPQCを併用し、段階的に移行する</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#shared-2-1\">実行環境と通信相手のPQC対応を確認する</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n</div>\n<details class=\"shared\"><summary>共通の確認・計画 (2)</summary>\n<section id=\"shared-2-0\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>既存方式とPQCを併用し、段階的に移行する <span class=\"badge\">早めに対応</span></h4><p>検出した方式には、量子計算による将来のリスクがあります。接続相手との互換性を確かめながら移行を進めてください。</p><ol>\n<li>利用箇所と担当チームを洗い出してください。</li>\n<li>既存のPQC・複合構成を確認し、移行が必要なら新旧方式の併用を試してください。</li>\n<li>旧方式を廃止する条件と時期を決めてください。</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>参考資料・変更例</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n</section>\n<section id=\"shared-2-1\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>実行環境と通信相手のPQC対応を確認する <span class=\"badge\">計画して対応</span></h4><p>コードに方式名があるだけでは、その環境で動くか、接続相手が対応しているかは分かりません。</p><ol>\n<li>JDK 24以降のML-KEM・ML-DSA対応を確認してください。プロバイダーや通信規約の対応は別に確認が必要です。</li>\n<li>実際に配備している版、プロバイダー、機能設定を確認してください。</li>\n<li>本番設定を変える前に、接続相手との互換性を試してください。</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>参考資料・変更例</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/27/security/java-secure-socket-extension-jsse-reference-guide.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/27/security/java-secure-socket-extension-jsse-reference-guide.html</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n</section>\n</details>\n</div></details>\n<details class=\"rule-card\" id=\"rule-3\" data-rule data-page-size=\"20\"><summary><span><strong>日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference</strong> <code>PKI056</code></span><span class=\"sev medium\">中</span><span class=\"count\">1 件</span><span>ファイル 1 / 表示対象 <span data-match-count></span></span></summary><div class=\"rule-body\"><p>ルール作成者の確認事項（原文）：Review actual use before migration</p>\n<h4>検出箇所と対応</h4><nav data-occ-pager hidden><button type=\"button\" data-occ-prev>前の箇所</button><span data-occ-status aria-live=\"polite\"></span><button type=\"button\" data-occ-next>次の箇所</button></nav><div data-occurrence-list>\n<details class=\"occurrence\" id=\"finding-3\" data-finding-id=\"PKI056\" data-inventory=\"false\" data-severity=\"medium\" data-risk=\"quantum-vulnerable\" data-search=\"PKI056 日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference certificate.pem\"><summary><code>certificate.pem:1:1</code><span class=\"occ-match\">synthetic reference</span><span class=\"next-step\">対応: ルール作成者の確認事項（原文）：Review actual use before migration</span></summary><p>判断の目安: 量子計算によるリスクあり</p><p>確認すること: ルール作成者の確認事項（原文）：Review actual use before migration</p><p>検出した記述: <code>synthetic reference</code></p>\n<p>周辺のコードは取得できませんでした。元のファイルを確認してください。</p>\n<h4>この箇所の対応</h4>\n<p>共通の確認・計画（この行で確認済みの事実ではありません）：</p><ul>\n<li><a href=\"#shared-3-0\">既存方式とPQCを併用し、段階的に移行する</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#shared-3-1\">証明書の発行と信頼設定の更新を計画する</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n</div>\n<details class=\"shared\"><summary>共通の確認・計画 (2)</summary>\n<section id=\"shared-3-0\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>既存方式とPQCを併用し、段階的に移行する <span class=\"badge\">早めに対応</span></h4><p>検出した方式には、量子計算による将来のリスクがあります。接続相手との互換性を確かめながら移行を進めてください。</p><ol>\n<li>利用箇所と担当チームを洗い出してください。</li>\n<li>既存のPQC・複合構成を確認し、移行が必要なら新旧方式の併用を試してください。</li>\n<li>旧方式を廃止する条件と時期を決めてください。</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>参考資料・変更例</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n</section>\n<section id=\"shared-3-1\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<section class=\"action\"><h4>証明書の発行と信頼設定の更新を計画する <span class=\"badge\">早めに対応</span></h4><p>FIPS 204/205は署名方式の規格であり、共通のハイブリッド証明書形式を定めていません。</p><ol>\n<li>CBOMで証明書の署名方式と鍵情報を確認してください。</li>\n<li>具体的な構成と符号化形式を選び、プロバイダー、認証局、クライアント、信頼ストアの対応を確認してから発行を計画してください。</li>\n<li>対応が確認できた構成だけを本番以外で試してください。形式や利用環境が非対応なら未検証のままとし、別の対応済みの移行方法を検討してください。</li>\n<li>ルート・中間・サーバー証明書の再発行手順を決めてください。</li>\n</ol>\n<details><summary>参考資料・変更例</summary>\n<p><a href=\"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/205/final\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/205/final</a></p>\n</details>\n</section>\n</section>\n</details>\n</div></details>\n</main><script>(() => {\n  const root = document.querySelector('[data-compact-report]');\n  if (!root) return;\n  const ja = document.documentElement.lang === 'ja';\n  const choose = (en, jp) => ja ? jp : en;\n  const controls = root.querySelector('[data-report-controls]');\n  const mode = controls.querySelector('[data-mode]');\n  const search = controls.querySelector('[data-search]');\n  const severity = controls.querySelector('[data-severity]');\n  const risk = controls.querySelector('[data-risk]');\n  const rules = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll('[data-rule]'));\n  const rows = new Map(rules.map(rule => [rule, Array.from(rule.querySelectorAll('[data-finding-id]'))]));\n  const pages = new Map();\n  let page = 0;\n  let visibleRules = [];\n  const matches = row => {\n    const inventory = row.dataset.inventory === 'true';\n    return (mode.value === 'all' || (mode.value === 'inventory' ? inventory : !inventory))\n      && (!severity.value || row.dataset.severity === severity.value)\n      && (!risk.value || row.dataset.risk === risk.value)\n      && row.dataset.search.toLocaleLowerCase().includes(search.value.trim().toLocaleLowerCase());\n  };\n  function refresh() {\n    let count = 0;\n    visibleRules = [];\n    for (const rule of rules) {\n      const all = rows.get(rule);\n      const matched = all.filter(matches);\n      count += matched.length;\n      if (matched.length) visibleRules.push(rule);\n      const last = Math.max(0, Math.ceil(matched.length / 20) - 1);\n      const p = Math.min(pages.get(rule) || 0, last);\n      pages.set(rule, p);\n      all.forEach(row => { const i = matched.indexOf(row); row.hidden = i < p * 20 || i >= (p + 1) * 20; });\n      rule.querySelector('[data-match-count]').textContent = `${matched.length} / ${all.length}`;\n      rule.querySelector('[data-occ-pager]').hidden = matched.length <= 20;\n      rule.querySelector('[data-occ-prev]').disabled = p === 0;\n      rule.querySelector('[data-occ-next]').disabled = p === last;\n      rule.querySelector('[data-occ-status]').textContent = `${matched.length ? p * 20 + 1 : 0}-${Math.min((p + 1) * 20, matched.length)} / ${matched.length}`;\n    }\n    const last = Math.max(0, Math.ceil(visibleRules.length / 20) - 1);\n    page = Math.min(page, last);\n    rules.forEach(rule => { const i = visibleRules.indexOf(rule); rule.hidden = i < page * 20 || i >= (page + 1) * 20; });\n    root.querySelector('[data-report-status]').textContent = choose(\n      `${visibleRules.length} / ${rules.length} rule groups; ${count} / ${Array.from(rows.values()).reduce((n,r) => n+r.length,0)} findings match the current view.`,\n      `表示対象：${visibleRules.length} / ${rules.length}ルール、${count} / ${Array.from(rows.values()).reduce((n,r) => n+r.length,0)}箇所`);\n    root.querySelector('[data-empty]').hidden = count !== 0;\n    root.querySelector('[data-group-pager]').hidden = visibleRules.length <= 20;\n    root.querySelector('[data-prev]').disabled = page === 0;\n    root.querySelector('[data-next]').disabled = page === last;\n    root.querySelector('[data-page]').textContent = `${visibleRules.length ? page * 20 + 1 : 0}-${Math.min((page + 1) * 20, visibleRules.length)} / ${visibleRules.length}`;\n  }\n  function reset() { mode.value = 'all'; search.value = ''; severity.value = ''; risk.value = ''; page = 0; pages.clear(); }\n  controls.hidden = false;\n  controls.addEventListener('input', () => {\n    if (severity.value === 'info' || risk.value === 'quantum-safe') mode.value = 'all';\n    page = 0; pages.clear(); refresh();\n  });\n  root.addEventListener('click', event => {\n    const button = event.target.closest('button');\n    if (!button || !root.contains(button)) return;\n    if (button.matches('[data-reset]')) reset();\n    else if (button.matches('[data-prev]')) page--;\n    else if (button.matches('[data-next]')) page++;\n    else if (button.matches('[data-occ-prev], [data-occ-next]')) {\n      const rule = button.closest('[data-rule]');\n      pages.set(rule, (pages.get(rule) || 0) + (button.matches('[data-occ-next]') ? 1 : -1));\n    } else return;\n    refresh();\n  });\n  function revealHash() {\n    let id;\n    try { id = decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1)); } catch { return; }\n    const target = document.getElementById(id);\n    if (!target || !root.contains(target)) return;\n    const rule = target.closest('[data-rule]');\n    if (!rule) return;\n    reset();\n    page = Math.floor(rules.indexOf(rule) / 20);\n    const occurrence = target.closest('[data-finding-id]');\n    if (occurrence) pages.set(rule, Math.floor(rows.get(rule).indexOf(occurrence) / 20));\n    refresh();\n    for (let element = target; element && element !== root; element = element.parentElement) {\n      if (element.tagName === 'DETAILS') element.open = true;\n    }\n    (target.querySelector('summary') || target).focus();\n    target.scrollIntoView({block: 'nearest'});\n  }\n  window.addEventListener('hashchange', revealHash);\n  refresh();\n  if (location.hash) revealHash();\n})();\n</script></body></html>\n","ja/report.json":"{\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-11-15T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"JAVA_UNKNOWN056\",\n      \"rule_id\": \"JAVA_UNKNOWN056\",\n      \"category\": \"CryptoAPI\",\n      \"risk\": \"quantum-vulnerable\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.8,\n      \"description\": \"Synthetic migration reference\",\n      \"migration_hint\": \"Review actual use before migration\",\n      \"location\": {\n        \"file\": \"unknown/Example.java\",\n        \"line\": 1,\n        \"column\": 1\n      },\n      \"evidence\": {\n        \"type\": \"configuration_match\",\n        \"match\": \"synthetic reference\",\n        \"snippet_preview\": \"synthetic reference\",\n        \"metadata\": {\n          \"scope\": \"config\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"recommended_actions\": [\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"plan.hybrid-migration\",\n          \"title\": \"Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan\",\n          \"priority\": \"near-term\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The detected primitive is vulnerable to cryptographically relevant quantum attacks. Hybrid rollout minimizes compatibility risk.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Inventory all call sites using this algorithm and owner teams.\",\n            \"Check for an existing classical + PQC composition; if migration is needed, evaluate compatible staged or hybrid modes before hard cut-over.\",\n            \"Define retirement dates for legacy classical algorithms.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"java.runtime-upgrade-for-pqc\",\n          \"title\": \"Check Java runtime baseline for standard PQC APIs\",\n          \"priority\": \"planned\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The Java version is unknown; verify the deployed runtime before selecting a PQC API baseline.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Target JDK 24+ for ML-KEM and ML-DSA support planning.\",\n            \"Pilot compatibility testing in CI before production migration.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://openjdk.org/jeps/496\",\n            \"https://openjdk.org/jeps/497\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"java.bouncycastle-pqc\",\n          \"title\": \"Provide BouncyCastle PQC fallback path\",\n          \"priority\": \"near-term\",\n          \"rationale\": \"BouncyCastle can be used as a pragmatic transition option when standard runtime support is unavailable or incomplete.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Verify the resolved BC release and deployed JDK support before provider initialization; the example uses BC Java 1.85 and the BC provider, not BCPQC.\",\n            \"Select explicit ML-DSA / ML-KEM parameter sets for the intended purpose. Generate new algorithm-compatible keys and provision matching public keys and encodings to verifiers; never reuse RSA key material.\",\n            \"Document provider ordering and FIPS/compliance impact.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://www.bouncycastle.org/java.html\",\n            \"https://downloads.bouncycastle.org/java/docs/bcprov-jdk18on-javadoc/\"\n          ],\n          \"code_examples\": [\n            {\n              \"language\": \"java\",\n              \"before\": \"Security.addProvider(new BouncyCastleProvider());\\nSignature sig = Signature.getInstance(\\\"SHA256withRSA\\\", \\\"BC\\\");\",\n              \"after\": \"// BC Java 1.85 example: verify the resolved release/provider supports this name.\\nSecurity.addProvider(new BouncyCastleProvider());\\n// Provision a new ML-DSA-65 key pair and its public key to verifiers.\\n// mlDsaPrivateKey must not be the previous RSA key.\\nSignature sig = Signature.getInstance(\\\"ML-DSA-65\\\", \\\"BC\\\");\\nsig.initSign(mlDsaPrivateKey);\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"runtime.verify-pqc-capabilities\",\n          \"title\": \"Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities\",\n          \"priority\": \"planned\",\n          \"rationale\": \"Source declarations and primitive availability do not establish deployment or peer support.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"JDK 24 adds ML-KEM and ML-DSA primitives. Check deployed JSSE hybrid TLS support separately and inspect jdk.tls.namedGroups restrictions.\",\n            \"Check resolved versions, provider/features and interoperability before changing production policy.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/27/security/java-secure-socket-extension-jsse-reference-guide.html\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"JAVA_CURRENT056\",\n      \"rule_id\": \"JAVA_CURRENT056\",\n      \"category\": \"CryptoAPI\",\n      \"risk\": \"quantum-vulnerable\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.8,\n      \"description\": \"Synthetic migration reference\",\n      \"migration_hint\": \"Review actual use before migration\",\n      \"location\": {\n        \"file\": \"current/Example.java\",\n        \"line\": 1,\n        \"column\": 1\n      },\n      \"evidence\": {\n        \"type\": \"configuration_match\",\n        \"match\": \"synthetic reference\",\n        \"snippet_preview\": \"synthetic reference\",\n        \"metadata\": {\n          \"scope\": \"config\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"recommended_actions\": [\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"plan.hybrid-migration\",\n          \"title\": \"Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan\",\n          \"priority\": \"near-term\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The detected primitive is vulnerable to cryptographically relevant quantum attacks. Hybrid rollout minimizes compatibility risk.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Inventory all call sites using this algorithm and owner teams.\",\n            \"Check for an existing classical + PQC composition; if migration is needed, evaluate compatible staged or hybrid modes before hard cut-over.\",\n            \"Define retirement dates for legacy classical algorithms.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"java.jca-ml-dsa-ml-kem\",\n          \"title\": \"Use Java standard JCA names for ML-DSA / ML-KEM\",\n          \"priority\": \"near-term\",\n          \"rationale\": \"Modern JDKs expose standardized PQC algorithm names through JCA, reducing vendor lock-in.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Select an explicit parameter set and generate a new ML-DSA key pair; never reuse RSA key material.\",\n            \"Provision matching public keys and required JOSE/PKI encodings to all verifiers before switching signers to ML-DSA where policy allows.\",\n            \"Adopt ML-KEM for key establishment in hybrid TLS/key exchange designs.\",\n            \"Keep dual verification during migration to preserve compatibility.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://openjdk.org/jeps/496\",\n            \"https://openjdk.org/jeps/497\"\n          ],\n          \"code_examples\": [\n            {\n              \"language\": \"java\",\n              \"before\": \"Signature sig = Signature.getInstance(\\\"SHA256withRSA\\\");\\nsig.initSign(privateKey);\\nsig.update(payload);\\nbyte[] signature = sig.sign();\",\n              \"after\": \"// JDK 24+: provision a new ML-DSA key pair for the selected parameter set.\\n// mlDsaPrivateKey is its private key, never the previous RSA key.\\n// Provision the matching public key and encoding to verifiers before rollout.\\nSignature sig = Signature.getInstance(\\\"ML-DSA\\\");\\nsig.initSign(mlDsaPrivateKey);\\nsig.update(payload);\\nbyte[] signature = sig.sign();\\n// Keep legacy verification only under the explicit migration policy.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"runtime.verify-pqc-capabilities\",\n          \"title\": \"Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities\",\n          \"priority\": \"planned\",\n          \"rationale\": \"Source declarations and primitive availability do not establish deployment or peer support.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"JDK 24 adds ML-KEM and ML-DSA primitives. Check deployed JSSE hybrid TLS support separately and inspect jdk.tls.namedGroups restrictions.\",\n            \"Check resolved versions, provider/features and interoperability before changing production policy.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/27/security/java-secure-socket-extension-jsse-reference-guide.html\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"PKI056\",\n      \"rule_id\": \"PKI056\",\n      \"category\": \"PKI\",\n      \"risk\": \"quantum-vulnerable\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.8,\n      \"description\": \"Synthetic migration reference\",\n      \"migration_hint\": \"Review actual use before migration\",\n      \"location\": {\n        \"file\": \"certificate.pem\",\n        \"line\": 1,\n        \"column\": 1\n      },\n      \"evidence\": {\n        \"type\": \"configuration_match\",\n        \"match\": \"synthetic reference\",\n        \"snippet_preview\": \"synthetic reference\",\n        \"metadata\": {\n          \"scope\": \"config\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"recommended_actions\": [\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"plan.hybrid-migration\",\n          \"title\": \"Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan\",\n          \"priority\": \"near-term\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The detected primitive is vulnerable to cryptographically relevant quantum attacks. Hybrid rollout minimizes compatibility risk.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Inventory all call sites using this algorithm and owner teams.\",\n            \"Check for an existing classical + PQC composition; if migration is needed, evaluate compatible staged or hybrid modes before hard cut-over.\",\n            \"Define retirement dates for legacy classical algorithms.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"pki.hybrid-certificate-roadmap\",\n          \"title\": \"Plan certificate algorithm and trust-store migration\",\n          \"priority\": \"near-term\",\n          \"rationale\": \"PKI updates require coordinated CA, chain, and relying-party compatibility planning. FIPS 204/205 standardize signature primitives, not a universal hybrid certificate format.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Inventory certificate signature algorithms and key sizes from CBOM/report output.\",\n            \"Identify the exact certificate construction and encoding, then verify provider, CA, client and trust-store support before planning issuance.\",\n            \"Pilot only a supported construction in non-production trust stores; if format or ecosystem support is unavailable, keep issuance unverified and evaluate another supported migration path.\",\n            \"Define reissuance plan for quantum-vulnerable roots/intermediates/end-entity certs.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/205/final\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"ENVOY056\",\n      \"rule_id\": \"ENVOY056\",\n      \"category\": \"TLS\",\n      \"risk\": \"quantum-vulnerable\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.8,\n      \"description\": \"Synthetic migration reference\",\n      \"migration_hint\": \"Review actual use before migration\",\n      \"location\": {\n        \"file\": \"envoy.yaml\",\n        \"line\": 1,\n        \"column\": 1\n      },\n      \"evidence\": {\n        \"type\": \"configuration_match\",\n        \"match\": \"synthetic reference\",\n        \"snippet_preview\": \"synthetic reference\",\n        \"metadata\": {\n          \"scope\": \"config\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"recommended_actions\": [\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"envoy.pqc-signature-readiness-note\",\n          \"title\": \"Validate Envoy PQC signature compatibility in control/data planes\",\n          \"priority\": \"advisory\",\n          \"rationale\": \"Envoy TLS behavior depends on configured providers and peer capabilities; PQC signature readiness can vary between mesh edges, sidecars, and external clients.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Harden min/max TLS versions and retire static RSA key exchange where configured; ECDHE_RSA uses RSA authentication, not static RSA key exchange.\",\n            \"Review cipher_suites for TLS 1.0-1.2, not TLS 1.3; review certificate signatures and peer compatibility separately.\",\n            \"Verify PQC certificate-signature compatibility in both downstream and upstream clusters.\",\n            \"Gate production rollout with staged canary tests and explicit fallback paths.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/intro/arch_overview/security/ssl.html\",\n            \"https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"plan.hybrid-migration\",\n          \"title\": \"Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan\",\n          \"priority\": \"near-term\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The detected primitive is vulnerable to cryptographically relevant quantum attacks. Hybrid rollout minimizes compatibility risk.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Inventory all call sites using this algorithm and owner teams.\",\n            \"Check for an existing classical + PQC composition; if migration is needed, evaluate compatible staged or hybrid modes before hard cut-over.\",\n            \"Define retirement dates for legacy classical algorithms.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final\",\n            \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"tls.remove-rsa-kex\",\n          \"title\": \"Prefer TLS 1.3 and review legacy key exchange\",\n          \"priority\": \"near-term\",\n          \"rationale\": \"RSA key exchange and legacy protocol versions are high-priority migration blockers for PQC readiness.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Prefer TLS 1.3; restrict connections to TLS 1.3 when all peers support it. Disable TLS 1.0 and 1.1.\",\n            \"Retain securely configured TLS 1.2 only where interoperability requires it, and record the compatibility reason.\",\n            \"Prefer ECDHE today and plan hybrid KEM suites for next phase.\",\n            \"Continuously test interoperability across clients and load balancers.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"action_id\": \"tls.envoy-hardening\",\n          \"title\": \"Set modern TLS policy in Envoy\",\n          \"priority\": \"near-term\",\n          \"rationale\": \"Envoy control-plane config supports strict min/max protocol and cipher suite policy.\",\n          \"steps\": [\n            \"Prefer `tls_minimum_protocol_version: TLSv1_3`; use TLSv1_2 only when interoperability requires it.\",\n            \"Review `cipher_suites` for TLS 1.0-1.2, not TLS 1.3. Retire static RSA key exchange where configured; ECDHE_RSA uses RSA authentication, not static RSA key exchange.\",\n            \"Review certificate-signature migration and peer compatibility separately before removing RSA authentication.\"\n          ],\n          \"references\": [\n            \"https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cbom\": [],\n  \"dependency_sbom\": [],\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"total_findings\": 4,\n    \"by_severity\": {\n      \"medium\": 4\n    },\n    \"by_risk\": {\n      \"quantum-vulnerable\": 4\n    },\n    \"scanned_files\": 4,\n    \"skipped_files\": 0\n  }\n}","ja/report.md":"# 耐量子暗号への移行調査レポート\n\n作成日時: 2026-11-15 00:00:00 UTC\n\n対応を確認する候補: 4 / 参考情報: 0 / 調査したファイル: 4\n\nコードや設定の手掛かりをまとめた調査結果です。\n\n|重大度|件数（全検出）|\n|---|---:|\n|中|4|\n\n## 対応候補の索引\n\n|ルール・説明|重大度|判断の目安|件数|ファイル数|\n|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n|[ENVOY056](#rule-0) 日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference|中|量子計算によるリスクあり|1|1|\n|[JAVA_CURRENT056](#rule-1) 日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference|中|量子計算によるリスクあり|1|1|\n|[JAVA_UNKNOWN056](#rule-2) 日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference|中|量子計算によるリスクあり|1|1|\n|[PKI056](#rule-3) 日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference|中|量子計算によるリスクあり|1|1|\n\n## 参考情報の索引\n\n|ルール・説明|重大度|判断の目安|件数|ファイル数|\n|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n\n<a id=\"rule-0\"></a>\n\n## ENVOY056\n\n日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference\n\n確認すること: ルール作成者の確認事項（原文）：Review actual use before migration\n\n|検出箇所|検出した記述|対応・詳細|\n|---|---|---|\n|<a id=\"finding-0\"></a>[envoy.yaml:1:1](#finding-0)|synthetic reference|TLS 1.3を優先し、鍵共有方式を確認する / [EnvoyのPQC証明書署名の互換性を確認する](#action-0) / [TLS 1.3を優先し、鍵共有方式を確認する](#action-2) / [EnvoyのTLS設定を見直す](#action-3) / 周辺コードなし|\n\nこのルールの全箇所に共通する確認・計画（各行で確認済みの事実ではありません）:\n\n- [既存方式とPQCを併用し、段階的に移行する](#action-1)\n\n<a id=\"rule-1\"></a>\n\n## JAVA_CURRENT056\n\n日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference\n\n確認すること: ルール作成者の確認事項（原文）：Review actual use before migration\n\n|検出箇所|検出した記述|対応・詳細|\n|---|---|---|\n|<a id=\"finding-1\"></a>[current/Example.java:1:1](#finding-1)|synthetic reference|Java標準のPQC APIへの移行を検討する / [Java標準のPQC APIへの移行を検討する](#action-4) / 周辺コードなし|\n\nこのルールの全箇所に共通する確認・計画（各行で確認済みの事実ではありません）:\n\n- [既存方式とPQCを併用し、段階的に移行する](#action-1)\n- [実行環境と通信相手のPQC対応を確認する](#action-5)\n\n<a id=\"rule-2\"></a>\n\n## JAVA_UNKNOWN056\n\n日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference\n\n確認すること: ルール作成者の確認事項（原文）：Review actual use before migration\n\n|検出箇所|検出した記述|対応・詳細|\n|---|---|---|\n|<a id=\"finding-2\"></a>[unknown/Example.java:1:1](#finding-2)|synthetic reference|BouncyCastleによるPQC対応を検討する / [Javaの版を確認し、必要ならPQC API対応版へ更新する](#action-6) / [BouncyCastleによるPQC対応を検討する](#action-7) / 周辺コードなし|\n\nこのルールの全箇所に共通する確認・計画（各行で確認済みの事実ではありません）:\n\n- [既存方式とPQCを併用し、段階的に移行する](#action-1)\n- [実行環境と通信相手のPQC対応を確認する](#action-5)\n\n<a id=\"rule-3\"></a>\n\n## PKI056\n\n日本語の説明が未登録のルールです。原文：Synthetic migration reference\n\n確認すること: ルール作成者の確認事項（原文）：Review actual use before migration\n\n|検出箇所|検出した記述|対応・詳細|\n|---|---|---|\n|<a id=\"finding-3\"></a>[certificate.pem:1:1](#finding-3)|synthetic reference|ルール作成者の確認事項（原文）：Review actual use before migration / 周辺コードなし|\n\nこのルールの全箇所に共通する確認・計画（各行で確認済みの事実ではありません）:\n\n- [既存方式とPQCを併用し、段階的に移行する](#action-1)\n- [証明書の発行と信頼設定の更新を計画する](#action-8)\n\n## 対応案の詳細\n\n各検出箇所から、その箇所に該当する対応案だけを参照します。同じ内容は一度だけ掲載します。\n\n<a id=\"action-0\"></a>\n\n\n#### EnvoyのPQC証明書署名の互換性を確認する (advisory)\n\n鍵共有と証明書の署名は別です。プロバイダーと通信相手の対応を確認してください。\n\n1. TLSの最低・最高バージョンを見直し、設定に静的RSA鍵交換があれば移行を検討してください。ECDHE_RSAのRSA認証とは区別してください。\n2. cipher_suitesはTLS 1.0〜1.2の設定で、TLS 1.3には適用されません。\n3. 下流・上流の両方でPQC証明書署名の互換性を試し、段階的な展開と切戻しを準備してください。\n\n参考資料:\n\n- https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/intro/arch_overview/security/ssl.html\n- https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto\n<a id=\"action-1\"></a>\n\n\n#### 既存方式とPQCを併用し、段階的に移行する (早めに対応)\n\n検出した方式には、量子計算による将来のリスクがあります。接続相手との互換性を確かめながら移行を進めてください。\n\n1. 利用箇所と担当チームを洗い出してください。\n2. 既存のPQC・複合構成を確認し、移行が必要なら新旧方式の併用を試してください。\n3. 旧方式を廃止する条件と時期を決めてください。\n\n参考資料:\n\n- https://www.nist.gov/itl/post-quantum-cryptography\n- https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final\n- https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\n<a id=\"action-2\"></a>\n\n\n#### TLS 1.3を優先し、鍵共有方式を確認する (早めに対応)\n\nRSA鍵交換や古いTLS設定は移行時の確認対象です。この一般的な確認項目だけで、RSAの利用が確定するわけではありません。\n\n1. TLS 1.3を優先し、全接続先が対応していれば1.3だけを許可してください。TLS 1.0・1.1は無効にしてください。\n2. TLS 1.2は互換性が必要な場合に限り、安全な設定で残してください。理由を記録し、鍵共有方式のPQC対応も別に確認してください。\n3. クライアントと負荷分散装置を含め、互換性を継続して確認してください。\n\n参考資料:\n\n- https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446\n<a id=\"action-3\"></a>\n\n\n#### EnvoyのTLS設定を見直す (早めに対応)\n\n最低・最高バージョンと暗号スイートを設定で管理できます。\n\n1. tls_minimum_protocol_versionはTLSv1_3を優先し、TLSv1_2は互換性が必要な場合に限って検討してください。\n2. cipher_suitesはTLS 1.0〜1.2の設定で、TLS 1.3には適用されません。静的RSA鍵交換と、ECDHE_RSAのRSA認証を区別してください。\n3. RSA認証を外す前に、証明書の署名方式と通信相手の互換性を別に確認してください。\n\n参考資料:\n\n- https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/extensions/transport_sockets/tls/v3/tls.proto\n<a id=\"action-4\"></a>\n\n\n#### Java標準のPQC APIへの移行を検討する (早めに対応)\n\n対応するJDKでは、JCAの標準方式名でML-DSA・ML-KEMを指定できます。\n\n1. パラメーターセットを選び、新しいML-DSA鍵ペアを生成してください。RSAの鍵を流用しないでください。\n2. 署名側を切り替える前に、対応する公開鍵とJOSE・PKIの符号化形式をすべての検証側へ配備してください。\n3. ML-KEMは鍵共有に使う方式です。TLSなどの対応は別に確認してください。\n4. 旧方式の検証を残す条件と廃止時期は、移行方針として明示してください。\n\n参考資料:\n\n- https://openjdk.org/jeps/496\n- https://openjdk.org/jeps/497\n\n変更前 (java)\n\n    Signature sig = Signature.getInstance(\"SHA256withRSA\");\n    sig.initSign(privateKey);\n    sig.update(payload);\n    byte[] signature = sig.sign();\n\n変更後\n\n    // JDK 24+: provision a new ML-DSA key pair for the selected parameter set.\n    // mlDsaPrivateKey is its private key, never the previous RSA key.\n    // Provision the matching public key and encoding to verifiers before rollout.\n    Signature sig = Signature.getInstance(\"ML-DSA\");\n    sig.initSign(mlDsaPrivateKey);\n    sig.update(payload);\n    byte[] signature = sig.sign();\n    // Keep legacy verification only under the explicit migration policy.\n\n<a id=\"action-5\"></a>\n\n\n#### 実行環境と通信相手のPQC対応を確認する (計画して対応)\n\nコードに方式名があるだけでは、その環境で動くか、接続相手が対応しているかは分かりません。\n\n1. JDK 24以降のML-KEM・ML-DSA対応を確認してください。プロバイダーや通信規約の対応は別に確認が必要です。\n2. 実際に配備している版、プロバイダー、機能設定を確認してください。\n3. 本番設定を変える前に、接続相手との互換性を試してください。\n\n参考資料:\n\n- https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/27/security/java-secure-socket-extension-jsse-reference-guide.html\n<a id=\"action-6\"></a>\n\n\n#### Javaの版を確認し、必要ならPQC API対応版へ更新する (計画して対応)\n\n版が不明な場合は、配備先のJavaを確認してください。宣言された版だけでは実環境のAPI対応は確定しません。\n\n1. 標準のML-KEM・ML-DSA APIが必要な場合は、JDK 24以降の対応を確認してください。\n2. 本番への適用前にCIで互換性を試してください。\n\n参考資料:\n\n- https://openjdk.org/jeps/496\n- https://openjdk.org/jeps/497\n<a id=\"action-7\"></a>\n\n\n#### BouncyCastleによるPQC対応を検討する (早めに対応)\n\n標準APIを使えない環境では、ライブラリによる対応が移行候補になります。\n\n1. 解決済みのBouncyCastleの版と配備先JDKの対応を確認してください。例はBC Java 1.85のBCプロバイダーを使います。BCPQCとは区別してください。\n2. 用途に合うパラメーターセットを選び、新しいML-DSA鍵ペアなど、方式に対応した鍵を生成してください。RSA鍵を流用せず、公開鍵と符号化形式を検証側へ配備してください。\n3. プロバイダーの優先順位とFIPSなどの運用要件への影響を記録してください。\n\n参考資料:\n\n- https://www.bouncycastle.org/java.html\n- https://downloads.bouncycastle.org/java/docs/bcprov-jdk18on-javadoc/\n\n変更前 (java)\n\n    Security.addProvider(new BouncyCastleProvider());\n    Signature sig = Signature.getInstance(\"SHA256withRSA\", \"BC\");\n\n変更後\n\n    // BC Java 1.85 example: verify the resolved release/provider supports this name.\n    Security.addProvider(new BouncyCastleProvider());\n    // Provision a new ML-DSA-65 key pair and its public key to verifiers.\n    // mlDsaPrivateKey must not be the previous RSA key.\n    Signature sig = Signature.getInstance(\"ML-DSA-65\", \"BC\");\n    sig.initSign(mlDsaPrivateKey);\n\n<a id=\"action-8\"></a>\n\n\n#### 証明書の発行と信頼設定の更新を計画する (早めに対応)\n\nFIPS 204/205は署名方式の規格であり、共通のハイブリッド証明書形式を定めていません。\n\n1. CBOMで証明書の署名方式と鍵情報を確認してください。\n2. 具体的な構成と符号化形式を選び、プロバイダー、認証局、クライアント、信頼ストアの対応を確認してから発行を計画してください。\n3. 対応が確認できた構成だけを本番以外で試してください。形式や利用環境が非対応なら未検証のままとし、別の対応済みの移行方法を検討してください。\n4. ルート・中間・サーバー証明書の再発行手順を決めてください。\n\n参考資料:\n\n- https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\n- https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/205/final\n\n## 棚卸しデータ\n\n- [CBOM](cbom.json): 0\n- [Dependency SBOM](dependency-sbom.json): 0\n\n","ja/report.sarif":"{\n  \"version\": \"2.1.0\",\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json\",\n  \"runs\": [\n    {\n      \"columnKind\": \"unicodeCodePoints\",\n      \"tool\": {\n        \"driver\": {\n          \"name\": \"pqc-scan\",\n          \"rules\": [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"ENVOY056\",\n              \"shortDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"TLS\"\n              },\n              \"fullDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference\"\n              },\n              \"defaultConfiguration\": {\n                \"level\": \"warning\"\n              }\n            },\n            {\n              \"id\": \"JAVA_CURRENT056\",\n              \"shortDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"CryptoAPI\"\n              },\n              \"fullDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference\"\n              },\n              \"defaultConfiguration\": {\n                \"level\": \"warning\"\n              }\n            },\n            {\n              \"id\": \"JAVA_UNKNOWN056\",\n              \"shortDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"CryptoAPI\"\n              },\n              \"fullDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference\"\n              },\n              \"defaultConfiguration\": {\n                \"level\": \"warning\"\n              }\n            },\n            {\n              \"id\": \"PKI056\",\n              \"shortDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"PKI\"\n              },\n              \"fullDescription\": {\n                \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference\"\n              },\n              \"defaultConfiguration\": {\n                \"level\": \"warning\"\n              }\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      },\n      \"results\": [\n        {\n          \"ruleId\": \"JAVA_UNKNOWN056\",\n          \"level\": \"warning\",\n          \"message\": {\n            \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference | migration_hint=Review actual use before migration | next_actions=Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term); Check Java runtime baseline for standard PQC APIs (planned); Provide BouncyCastle PQC fallback path (near-term); Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities (planned)\"\n          },\n          \"locations\": [\n            {\n              \"physicalLocation\": {\n                \"artifactLocation\": {\n                  \"uri\": \"unknown/Example.java\"\n                },\n                \"region\": {\n                  \"startLine\": 1,\n                  \"startColumn\": 1\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          ],\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"migration_hint\": \"Review actual use before migration\",\n            \"recommended_actions\": [\n              \"Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term)\",\n              \"Check Java runtime baseline for standard PQC APIs (planned)\",\n              \"Provide BouncyCastle PQC fallback path (near-term)\",\n              \"Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities (planned)\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"ruleId\": \"JAVA_CURRENT056\",\n          \"level\": \"warning\",\n          \"message\": {\n            \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference | migration_hint=Review actual use before migration | next_actions=Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term); Use Java standard JCA names for ML-DSA / ML-KEM (near-term); Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities (planned)\"\n          },\n          \"locations\": [\n            {\n              \"physicalLocation\": {\n                \"artifactLocation\": {\n                  \"uri\": \"current/Example.java\"\n                },\n                \"region\": {\n                  \"startLine\": 1,\n                  \"startColumn\": 1\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          ],\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"migration_hint\": \"Review actual use before migration\",\n            \"recommended_actions\": [\n              \"Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term)\",\n              \"Use Java standard JCA names for ML-DSA / ML-KEM (near-term)\",\n              \"Verify deployed runtime and protocol PQC capabilities (planned)\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"ruleId\": \"PKI056\",\n          \"level\": \"warning\",\n          \"message\": {\n            \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference | migration_hint=Review actual use before migration | next_actions=Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term); Plan certificate algorithm and trust-store migration (near-term)\"\n          },\n          \"locations\": [\n            {\n              \"physicalLocation\": {\n                \"artifactLocation\": {\n                  \"uri\": \"certificate.pem\"\n                },\n                \"region\": {\n                  \"startLine\": 1,\n                  \"startColumn\": 1\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          ],\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"migration_hint\": \"Review actual use before migration\",\n            \"recommended_actions\": [\n              \"Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term)\",\n              \"Plan certificate algorithm and trust-store migration (near-term)\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"ruleId\": \"ENVOY056\",\n          \"level\": \"warning\",\n          \"message\": {\n            \"text\": \"Synthetic migration reference | migration_hint=Review actual use before migration | next_actions=Validate Envoy PQC signature compatibility in control/data planes (advisory); Adopt a phased hybrid PQC migration plan (near-term); Prefer TLS 1.3 and review legacy key exchange (near-term); Set modern TLS policy in Envoy (near-term)\"\n          },\n          \"locations\": [\n            {\n              \"physicalLocation\": {\n                \"artifactLocation\": {\n                  \"uri\": \"envoy.yaml\"\n                },\n                \"region\": {\n                  \"startLine\": 1,\n                  \"startColumn\": 1\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          ],\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"migration_hint\": \"Review actual use before migration\",\n            \"recommended_actions\": [\n     